      "artist": "Drawn by Arthur J. Stansbury. Engraved by Rawdon, Clark &amp; Co.",
      "description": "Caption reads: \"VIEW OF BROADWAY NEAR GRACE CHURCH.\"\nCredit line reads: \"A. J. Stansbury. Rawdon, Clark &amp; Co. Sc.\"\nText (p. 217) reads: \"Was erected in 1809, as an independent church. It is a substantial and neat edifice of brick, with a handsome cupola; the rear of the building is in elliptical form, with a terraced garden, and the Rector's house adjoining.…\"\n\nAt center, the steeple of the second Trinity Church.",
